{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_013HdNKBHwcKujpzdBHnMMFf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the member document `anchor_gui.py`, here is the grounded summary:\n\n## Session Summary â€” Deliverable: `anchor_gui.py`\n\n**What it is**\n- `anchor_gui.py` is the primary Anchor application: a single-file, ~7,248-line Python HTTP server that generates and serves the full dashboard HTML on every request.\n- It depends only on the Python standard library for its HTTP/parsing/runtime core (`json`, `os`, `re`, `socket`, `threading`, `http.server`, `urllib.parse`, `html`, etc.), consistent with the stdlib-only rule.\n- All paths are rooted via `ANCHOR_DIR = _paths.CODE_DIR`, and it composes a large set of sibling Anchor modules (`rnd_registry`, `effort_history`, `sessions`, `summarizer`, `deliverables`, `job_runner`, `gate_adapter`, `brownfield_scan`, `terminal_session`, `handoff`, `preview_server`, etc.) rather than forking their logic.\n\n**Markdown/task layer (the productivity core)**\n- Parses markdown into Python dicts via `parse_tasks_from_md`, `parse_projects_from_md`, `parse_inbox_from_md`, `parse_archived_tasks`, and aggregates everything through `gather_all()`.\n- Implements the full task lifecycle as change operations: `mark_done`/`mark_undone`, `add_task`, `capture_inbox`, `edit_task`, `edit_project`, `cancel_task`, `save_for_later`, `restore_task`, and `link_task` â€” all guarded by a `_with_write_lock` decorator and logged via `log_change`.\n- Exposes these as POST endpoints (`/api/done`, `/api/undone`, `/api/add`, `/api/capture`, `/api/edit_task`, `/api/edit_project`, `/api/promote_*`/`demote_*`, `/api/cancel`, `/api/save_for_later`, `/api/restore`) plus a `GET /api/status` JSON summary.\n\n**R&D control surface (v2 + v3 \"Mission Control\")**\n- Renders the rich project window (`render_project_window_html`) and the Kanban/lane/session views (`_render_kanban_html`, `_render_lane_sessions`, `render_project_tile_html`), with the project-window JS held in a single-brace RAW string section.\n- v2 R&D POST endpoints are routed in `do_POST`: project lifecycle (`new_project`/`open_project`/`rescan`/`set_priority`/`archive_project`/`future_project`/`retire_project`/`reactivate_project`/`set_notes`/`set_blurb`/`link_task`), `launch_lane`, `answer_gate`, the persistent-terminal trio (`start_terminal`/`term_input`/`term_discover`/`term_adopt`), `cancel_job`, deliverables (`pin_deliverable`/`run_deliverable`), `regenerate_summary`, `add_idea`, and `promote_inbox`.\n- v3 ConPTY terminal transport is hand-rolled in-file: an RFC-6455 WebSocket codec (`ws_accept_key`, `encode_text_frame`, `encode_close_frame`, `encode_pong_frame`, `decode_frames`) backing `GET /api/rnd/term_ws`, with an SSE-out + POST-in fallback (`term_stream2`/`term_input2`) and `term_start`/`term_kill`/`term_resize` lifecycle endpoints.\n- v3 proactive features are wired through read-only GET endpoints (`/api/rnd/session_summary`, `/api/rnd/handoff_proposal`, `/api/rnd/previews`, `/api/rnd/term_sessions`) plus POST preview control (`preview_start`/`preview_stop`); summary generation is triggered in background via `_trigger_project_summary`/`_trigger_session_summary` so the render path never runs the model synchronously.\n- Serves brand/vendor static assets through traversal-guarded routes (`brand_asset`, `xterm_asset`, `anchor_term_asset`, with `_unsafe_path_seg` segment checks).\n\n**Runtime / hosting**\n- Cache-busting is driven by `_compute_build_id`/`cache_bust_script`, and a `_heartbeat_watchdog` thread backs the heartbeat endpoint.\n- The server enforces single-instance ownership of port 8777 via `_ExclusiveThreadingHTTPServer` + `make_server(host=\"127.0.0.1\", port=8777)` and `resolve_bind_host`, matching the documented `SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE` single-instance guard; `main()` is the entrypoint run as the persistent NSSM `anchor` service.\n\n**Grounding notes**\n- All claims above are drawn directly from definitions, imports, and route handlers present in `anchor_gui.py`. No run metrics (tokens/wall-clock) are available from the member document, so none are asserted."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1095,"cache_read_input_tokens":50959,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1095},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e546c99e-e794-4045-9671-222839b8923f","uuid":"578c4930-8e54-4e6e-9c3c-c52d0e3590c7","request_id":"req_011CbyGwZmvxrMsxMDzfki5v"}
